### =============================================
### SAGA DEMO - Advanced Workflow Patterns
### =============================================
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates saga pattern with compensation, continue-as-new,
###          and multi-level parent-child-grandchild workflows
### AUDIENCE: Perfect for showcasing advanced Dapr workflow capabilities
### KEY FEATURE: Input-driven failure control for repeatable demos
### DURATION: Allow 10-15 minutes for full demonstration
### =============================================

### =============================================
### PHASE 1: SYSTEM PREPARATION
### =============================================

### 1. Health check for saga-demo service
GET http://localhost:3009/healthz

### 2. Restock inventory before demo
POST http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory/restock

### 3. Check inventory levels
GET http://localhost:3013/api/v1/inventory

### =============================================
### PHASE 2: SAGA PATTERN - Successful Order
### =============================================

### 4. Submit a successful saga order
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates complete saga flow without failures
### EXPECTED: reserve -> charge -> ship (all succeed)
### MONITORING: Watch for [SAGA] prefixed messages in notifications UI
// @name saga_success
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Alice",
    "item": "laptop",
    "total": 999.99,
    "destination": "123 Main Street, Suite 100"
}

### 5. Check saga order status
@saga_success_id = {{saga_success.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/saga/orders/{{saga_success_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 3: SAGA PATTERN - Failure at RESERVE Step
### =============================================

### 6. Submit order that fails at RESERVE step
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates early failure (no compensations needed)
### EXPECTED: reserve fails -> no steps to compensate
// @name saga_fail_reserve
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Bob",
    "item": "phone",
    "total": 599.99,
    "destination": "456 Oak Avenue",
    "fail_at_step": "reserve",
    "fail_type": "error",
    "simulate_delay_ms": 500
}

### 7. Check failed saga status
@saga_fail_reserve_id = {{saga_fail_reserve.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/saga/orders/{{saga_fail_reserve_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 4: SAGA PATTERN - Failure at CHARGE Step
### =============================================

### 8. Submit order that fails at CHARGE step
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates compensation for inventory reservation
### EXPECTED: reserve succeeds -> charge fails -> release_inventory compensation
// @name saga_fail_charge
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Carol",
    "item": "tablet",
    "total": 399.99,
    "destination": "789 Pine Road",
    "fail_at_step": "charge",
    "fail_type": "unavailable",
    "simulate_delay_ms": 1000
}

### 9. Check compensation execution
@saga_fail_charge_id = {{saga_fail_charge.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/saga/orders/{{saga_fail_charge_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 5: SAGA PATTERN - Failure at SHIP Step
### =============================================

### 10. Submit order that fails at SHIP step (full compensation)
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates full compensation chain
### EXPECTED: reserve -> charge -> ship fails -> refund_payment -> release_inventory
// @name saga_fail_ship
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "David",
    "item": "monitor",
    "total": 299.99,
    "destination": "321 Elm Boulevard",
    "fail_at_step": "ship",
    "fail_type": "timeout",
    "simulate_delay_ms": 500
}

### 11. Check full compensation chain
@saga_fail_ship_id = {{saga_fail_ship.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/saga/orders/{{saga_fail_ship_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 6: SAGA PATTERN - Force Success
### =============================================

### 12. Submit order with force_success flag
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates bypassing configured failures
### EXPECTED: All steps succeed despite any failure config
// @name saga_force_success
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Eve",
    "item": "keyboard",
    "total": 149.99,
    "destination": "555 Tech Lane",
    "fail_at_step": "charge",
    "fail_type": "error",
    "force_success": true
}

### 13. Verify forced success
@saga_force_success_id = {{saga_force_success.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/saga/orders/{{saga_force_success_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 7: CONTINUE-AS-NEW PATTERN
### =============================================

### 14. Start order monitoring workflow
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates continue-as-new for history management
### EXPECTED: Monitor runs multiple iterations, resetting history each time
// @name monitor_start
POST http://localhost:3009/monitor/start
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "order_id": "saga_alice_xxxxx",
    "check_interval_seconds": 3,
    "max_checks": 5
}

### 15. Check monitor status
@monitor_id = {{monitor_start.response.body.monitor_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/monitor/{{monitor_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 8: MULTI-LEVEL WORKFLOWS (Parent -> Child -> Grandchild)
### =============================================

### 16. Submit fulfillment order with workflow hierarchy
### PURPOSE: Demonstrates multi-level parent-child-grandchild workflows
### HIERARCHY:
###   - fulfill_xxx (Parent: Fulfillment)
###     - fulfill_xxx_validation (Child: Validation)
###       - fulfill_xxx_address_check (Grandchild: parallel)
###       - fulfill_xxx_payment_check (Grandchild: parallel)
// @name fulfillment_order
POST http://localhost:3009/fulfillment/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Frank",
    "item": "headphones",
    "total": 199.99,
    "destination": "888 Audio Drive, Building C"
}

### 17. Check fulfillment status (shows workflow hierarchy)
@fulfillment_id = {{fulfillment_order.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/fulfillment/orders/{{fulfillment_id}}

### 18. Submit another fulfillment to see parallel grandchild execution
// @name fulfillment_order_2
POST http://localhost:3009/fulfillment/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "Grace",
    "item": "webcam",
    "total": 89.99,
    "destination": "999 Video Street"
}

### 19. Check second fulfillment
@fulfillment_2_id = {{fulfillment_order_2.response.body.instance_id}}

GET http://localhost:3009/fulfillment/orders/{{fulfillment_2_id}}

### =============================================
### PHASE 9: RERUN DEMOS - Same Input, Different Outcomes
### =============================================

### 20. First run: Success
// @name rerun_demo_success
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "RerunTest",
    "item": "speaker",
    "total": 249.99,
    "destination": "111 Demo Lane"
}

### 21. Second run: Same customer, fail at charge
// @name rerun_demo_fail
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "RerunTest",
    "item": "speaker",
    "total": 249.99,
    "destination": "111 Demo Lane",
    "fail_at_step": "charge",
    "fail_type": "error"
}

### 22. Third run: Force success to recover
// @name rerun_demo_recover
POST http://localhost:3009/saga/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "customer": "RerunTest",
    "item": "speaker",
    "total": 249.99,
    "destination": "111 Demo Lane",
    "force_success": true
}

### =============================================
### DEMONSTRATION POINTS
### =============================================
###
### KEY FEATURES TO HIGHLIGHT:
###
### 1. SAGA PATTERN WITH COMPENSATION:
###    - Each step has explicit compensating action
###    - Compensations execute in reverse order on failure
###    - Clear visibility of rollback in notifications
###
### 2. INPUT-DRIVEN FAILURE CONTROL:
###    - fail_at_step: "reserve", "charge", "ship"
###    - fail_type: "timeout", "error", "unavailable"
###    - simulate_delay_ms: slow execution for visualization
###    - force_success: bypass failures for recovery demos
###
### 3. CONTINUE-AS-NEW PATTERN:
###    - Monitor workflow resets history each iteration
###    - Prevents unbounded history growth
###    - Shows long-running workflow management
###
### 4. MULTI-LEVEL WORKFLOW HIERARCHY:
###    - Parent: Fulfillment workflow
###    - Child: Validation workflow
###    - Grandchildren: Address + Payment checks (parallel)
###    - Uses when_all for parallel grandchild execution
###
### 5. RERUNNABLE WORKFLOWS:
###    - Same customer/item, different failure configs
###    - Perfect for Catalyst UI demonstrations
###    - Shows deterministic vs. dynamic behavior
###
### =============================================
### DEMO EXECUTION GUIDE:
###
### PREPARATION:
###   1. Run health check and restock inventory
###   2. Open notifications UI at localhost:8080
###   3. Open Catalyst UI for workflow visualization
###
### SAGA DEMO FLOW:
###   1. Start with successful order (Phase 2)
###   2. Show failure at each step progressively (Phases 3-5)
###   3. Demonstrate force_success recovery (Phase 6)
###
### CONTINUE-AS-NEW DEMO:
###   1. Start monitor and wait for iterations
###   2. Show history resets in Catalyst UI
###
### MULTI-LEVEL DEMO:
###   1. Submit fulfillment order
###   2. Show hierarchy in Catalyst UI
###   3. Watch parallel grandchild execution
###
### RERUN DEMO:
###   1. Run same order 3 times with different configs
###   2. Compare outcomes in Catalyst UI
###
### EXPECTED DURATION: 10-15 minutes
### NOTIFICATION RATE: 5-15 events per workflow
### =============================================
